{"timestamp":"2026-05-30T03:36:05.767Z","level":"info","source":"model","message":"response","data":{"model":"qwen36-35b","text":"\n\nI've loaded the **VoidRift Blueprint** (`blueprint.md`). Here's a summary of what this document covers:\n\n---\n\n## VoidRift: Decoupled Subsystem Architecture\n\n### What It Is\nVoidRift is a **highly decoupled, model-agnostic monorepo AI engineering harness** — a local developer tool combining a multi-agent orchestrator with an interactive Terminal User Interface (TUI) built in React and Ink.\n\n### Core Philosophy\n- **Local-First & Model Agnostic**: Runs local open-weight models (Ollama, vLLM, Llama.cpp) and cloud models (DeepSeek, Gemini, Anthropic, OpenAI)\n- **Rate-Limit & Cost Freedom**: 100-turn loops locally for $0 with zero rate-limit anxiety\n- **Sovereign Developer**: An engineering tool, not a toy — puts control in the operator's hands\n\n### Five Architectural Pillars\n1. **Pure Composition Root & Event Bus** — Parallel systems communicate via a central async Event Bus\n2. **Three-Partition Context** — Governance (static), Workspace (semi-dynamic), Work (volatile) for up to 90% prompt","toolCalls":[],"usage":{"promptTokens":4687,"completionTokens":672,"totalTokens":5359}}}
